title: "Make points originating from parachain consensus configurable"
doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      `RewardValidatorsWithEraPoints` now takes a third type parameter, `PointsPerWork: Get<u32>`,
      which is the amount of era points given per unit of parachain consensus work. Previously
      these were hardcoded through the `BACKING_POINTS` and `DISPUTE_STATEMENT_POINTS` constants,
      which are now removed.

      The unit of work depends on where the type is used: backing an included candidate when set
      as `inclusion::Config::RewardValidators`, and casting a dispute statement when set as
      `disputes::Config::RewardValidators`. Use a separate `PointsPerWork` for each to reward them
      differently, e.g. from `pallet-parameters`.

      To keep the previous behaviour, use `ConstU32<20>` for both:
      `RewardValidatorsWithEraPoints<Runtime, StakingAhClient, ConstU32<20>>`.

crates:
  - name: polkadot-runtime-parachains
    bump: major
  - name: westend-runtime
    bump: patch
